# What the push button does in `rp_button.s`: the number of instructions that
# the program has finished before the button moves, and its new level.

# A press that the program finds by asking
300,down
600,up

# A press that wakes the program with an interrupt. It comes soon after the
# program has gone to sleep: a sleeping program finishes instructions only
# when the timer wakes it, and on the chip's own time the timer does that
# once in 16 million clocks.
700,down
720,up
